Details:
In a context of website with Rerender code:    Kameleoon RWEP function is executed only once, after the CSS selector has been found in the DOM tree.   This is not OK when a website create and delete the HTML continuously has it is on recent framework such has REACT.   A good evolution would be to add a option in the RWEP function to run the code continuously    Basically, with existing RWEP function, we have this function to make it work that way :  const dynamicRWEP = (selector, callback, ) => {
    Kameleoon.API.Core.runWhenElementPresent(selector,(elements) => {
        elements.forEach(element => {
            element.classList.add('kameleoonRWEP1234');
        })
        //My Callback
        elements.forEach(element => {
            console.log("Play RWEP");
        })
        //End of my callback
        //Relaunch of the RWEP for new elements
        //Invisible with the evolution parameter "dynamicRefresh=true"
        dynamicRWEP();
    })
}

The website is dynamical.  CustomData are currently used as criteria in the segmentation for different purposes. Examples :    Status (connected or not connected)   number of games played (incremental)    Those Customdata are dynamical within the same page (no reloading of the page of reload of Kameleoon).  Need :    Being able to target with a customData with the current value (and not only the one when Kameleoon loaded)    Examples of UC :    I want to target a user as soon as he logged in.   I want to target a user from it 6th game played   I want to target a user as soon as it "money left" is under a certain amount    Idea how to :    In the segmentBuilder, when adding a CustomData criteria, being able to indicate that the value should be constantly evaluated until true (and then never stop on false)    How it is managed today :
- When the CD is updated, the following code is executed to restart the evaluation of all segment let mySegments = Kameleoon.API.Segments.getAll();
mySegments.forEach((segment) => {
   Kameleoon.API.Segments.reevaluate(segment.id);
})

