I think we need to create an API command for debugging. For example, we have code that checks for an element on the page, and if that element is not found, we write the following line in the code: Kameleoon.API.Core.messageInBo("Element not found on the page"). This would be very helpful for support, for instance:
- when the client changes the website structure, and the required element is missing from the page;
- when one test breaks the logic of another, and instead of `console.log` we call our function to send a message;
- when the requests start coming in incorrectly, and we also send information about the error;
In the back office, this would look as follows: upon entering the page, there would be a new tab with these messages and a link to the test or global code where this message was triggered.

